      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Joshua,\n\nI understand self-signed provider automatically issued the certificates but the library itself should not ask for regeneration of certificates with upgrade of library.\nTake the case of manual-tls-certificates, if the upgrade to new tls-certificates lirary resulted in regenerating new CSRs, the certificates should be regenerated by the operator and provide them back which is not expected.\n\nI raised a bug on https://github.com/canonical/tls-certificates-interface/issues/493 (OR) https://github.com/canonical/charmlibs/issues/565 and we cannot upgrade an existing deployment without regeneration of certificates until this is fixed.\n\nWe should hold merging this PR until the above issue is fixed in tls-certificates-interface library",
      "parentUuid": "96eec108_e73340b7",
      "revId": "c5e519418cef57c3403fb961c2b89dd60e44a611",
